### End-to-end scale-to-zero walkthrough
# Run these top to bottom against the dev stack:
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d --build
#
# The actual database connection is TCP (psql), not HTTP, so it cannot live in
# this file — the shell step is noted inline where it belongs.

@host = {{host}}

### 1. Provision. Comes back status "stopped": volume made, compute off.
POST {{host}}/api/{{engine}}/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{dbName}}",
  "username": "{{dbUser}}",
  "password": "{{dbPassword}}"
}

### 2. Confirm it is scaled to zero (status: stopped)
GET {{host}}/api/databases
Accept: application/json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Connect with psql. THIS is what wakes the compute. Run in a shell:
#
#    psql postgres://haki:hunter2@localhost:5432/mydb -c 'select 1;'
#
#    First connect pays the wake cost, then serves. Re-check status below and
#    it will read "running".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4. After connecting, status is now running
GET {{host}}/api/databases
Accept: application/json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Wait out IDLE_TIMEOUT (30s in the dev stack) with no connection, then
#    re-check. The reaper scales it back to "stopped". Watch the container
#    disappear in a shell:
#
#    docker ps        # sparkdb-postgres-mydb vanishes after ~30s idle
#    docker volume ls | grep sparkdb   # the volume survives
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 6. Back to stopped after idle
GET {{host}}/api/databases
Accept: application/json

### 7. Clean up (DESTRUCTIVE: drops the volume too)
POST {{host}}/api/{{engine}}/delete
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "{{dbName}}" }
